{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>You stretched out Your right hand — the earth swallowed them.</b> There is an allusion to what our Sages of blessed memory said (Sotah 11a): once the Egyptians took note of them [the Israelites who did not circumcise], they sought to kill them, and a miracle was done for them and they were swallowed into the ground, and afterward they would bud forth and rise and come home, flock by flock, etc. And at the sea they recognized Him first and said, ״זֶה אֵלִי״ (Exodus 15:2), and concerning this He said, ״עֹשֵׂה פֶלֶא״ (Exodus 15:11) — and what is the פֶּלֶא? ״נָטִיתָ יְמִינְךָ תִּבְלָעֵמוֹ אָרֶץ״ — concerning Israel, whom He mentioned in the verse ״מִי כָמֹכָה בָּאֵלִם ה׳״ (Exodus 15:11), and afterward, ״נָחִיתָ בְחַסְדְּךָ עַם זוּ גָּאָלְתָּ״ (Exodus 15:13), for they went home flock by flock, and afterward, ״נֵהַלְתָּ בְעָזְּךָ אֶל נְוֵה קָדְשֶׁךָ״ (Exodus 15:13), for they recognized Him first and saw the Shekhinah in the abode of His holiness, blessed be He." "And some say that this was said in the manner of question and answer: Why did You, O YHWH, bring the Egyptians into the Sea of Reeds to drown them there? And had You wished to stretch out Your hand against them, would the earth not have swallowed them in their place, like Korah's company? And He gave an answer to the matter: ״נָחִיתָ בְחַסְדְּךָ עַם זוּ גָּאָלְתָּ, נֵהַלְתָּ בְעָזְּךָ״ — as a shepherd guides his flock to a broad, lush pasture without the distress of war. For when they came out of Egypt they were not trained in warfare; therefore He brought them to the Sea of Reeds, whose roar resounded from one end of the world to the other, and through this ״שָׁמְעוּ עַמִּים יִרְגָּזוּן״, and they did not need to wage great wars — as it is written (Joshua 2:9), ״וְכִי נָמֹגוּ כָּל יוֹשְׁבֵי הָאָרֶץ מִפְּנֵיכֶם, כִּי שָׁמַעְנוּ אֵת אֲשֶׁר הוֹבִישׁ ה׳ מֵי יַם סוּף מִפְּנֵיכֶם״. But had they been swallowed into the ground in their place, the sound would not have been heard from afar, and all the kings of Canaan would not have trembled and quaked, and Israel would have needed to wage great wars."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:20:31.819450750Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}